    "id": 43,
    "topic": "Mata (Oftalmologi)",
    "question": "A 40-year-old man comes to the hospital outpatient clinic with swelling and redness of the left upper eyelid since 3 days ago. Since 2 hours ago, he complains of pus discharge from that area. The complaint is accompanied by fever and pain. There is no limitation of movement. The patient was hospitalized, and orbital CT scan with paranasal sinus extension showed no subperiosteal abscess and no sinusitis. The patient has a systemic history of diabetes since a young age. What is the most common etiology causing the condition in this case?",
    "options": [
      "A. Aspergillus fumigatus",
      "B. Propionibacterium acnes",
      "C. Staphylococcus aureus",
      "D. Pseudomonas aeruginosa",
      "E. Candida albicans"
    ],
